<title>BRAZIL: Brazil lengthens forex pact term for importers.</title>
<headline>Brazil lengthens forex pact term for importers.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank has lengthened the maximum period for the liquidation of foreign exchange contracts taken out by importers to 360 from 180 days, a Central Bank official said.</p>
<p>The move was taken to offer the 360-day term, which was previously available to importers of some specialist goods, to all Brazilian importers, Jose Maria Ferreira Carvalho, head of the bank's exchange department, told reporters.</p>
<p>Carvalho said the change was merely bureaucratic and would not have any impact on Brazil's trade balance. One effect, however, might be to better protect importers against exchange rate fluctuations, he said.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
